# Ferrite local environment — copied to $FERRITE_HOME/env.local (default
# ~/.local/share/ferrite/env.local) by scripts/setup-local.sh the first time,
# and never overwritten afterwards. Edit the copy, not this template.
#
# Format: plain KEY=VALUE, one per line. It is READ AS DATA by
# scripts/run-local.sh and scripts/doctor.sh, never `source`d, so nothing here
# is evaluated: no $VARIABLES, no $(commands), no escapes. Quote a value with
# "..." or '...' if it has spaces; '#' starts a comment only after whitespace.
#
# Only these key families are read (anything else is ignored with a warning):
#   FERRITE_*   OLLAMA_*   GEMINI_*   RUST_LOG
#
# A variable already exported in your shell WINS over this file, so
#   FERRITE_DEFENSE=off just run-local
# does what it says for that one run.
#
# NO SECRETS IN THIS FILE. API keys come from your shell environment or the OS
# keychain (see the end of this file) — the app's own rule is "environment or
# keyring, nowhere else" (crates/ferrite-model/src/secret.rs).

# ── Model tags (REQUIRED to run the agent) ────────────────────────────────
# No model name is ever a default (Ollama retires cloud models). List the tags
# your key can actually reach with `just models`, then set both. They may be
# the same tag.
# FERRITE_MODEL_SMALL=
# FERRITE_MODEL_MAIN=

# ── Model endpoint ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Default is Ollama Cloud (https://ollama.com), which needs OLLAMA_API_KEY.
# For a local Ollama instead (no key needed):
# FERRITE_OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
#
# Other model-layer knobs, all optional (defaults in
# crates/ferrite-model/src/config.rs):
# FERRITE_MODEL_CALL_BUDGET=500
# FERRITE_MODEL_MAX_IN_FLIGHT=2
# FERRITE_MODEL_TIMEOUT_SECS=60
# FERRITE_MODEL_CACHE_DIR=

# ── Defense mode ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Read once at startup by the tool-decision engine. Unset (or any
# unrecognised value) = full defense. The other values are for ablations only:
# off, sanitizer_only, loop_only.
# FERRITE_DEFENSE=on

# ── Laya decision server (OPTIONAL) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Laya is a small local decision model. When the app is given a URL it asks
# Laya "which operation, which element" for each browser step; with no URL the
# app runs exactly as before (LLM only). scripts/run-local.sh starts a local
# server for you on 127.0.0.1 unless you pass --no-laya.
#
# Point the app at a Laya server you run yourself (run-local then will NOT
# start one). Leave unset to let run-local manage a local one:
# FERRITE_LAYA_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8765
#
# Managed local server (scripts/laya/serve.py):
# FERRITE_LAYA_HOST=127.0.0.1        # loopback only by default; a non-loopback
#                                    #   host is refused unless an API key is set
# FERRITE_LAYA_PORT=8765
# FERRITE_LAYA_CHECKPOINT=v10s       # v10s = 322M, faster; v10 = 421M
# FERRITE_LAYA_DEVICE=               # empty = auto (cuda, then Apple mps, then cpu); or mps/cuda/cpu
# FERRITE_LAYA_THREADS=              # CPU only: cap torch threads (<= physical cores)
# FERRITE_LAYA_HEAD_MAX_LEN=         # empty = the checkpoint's own head_max_len_train (768)
# FERRITE_LAYA_LOG_LEVEL=info
# FERRITE_LAYA_OFFLINE=0             # 1 = never contact the Hugging Face Hub at start-up
#
# Bearer key for the Laya server. Not a model-provider secret, but treat it
# like one: export it in your shell instead of writing it here.
#   export FERRITE_LAYA_API_KEY=...

# ── Logging ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RUST_LOG=info

# ── API keys: environment or keychain, never this file ────────────────────
#   export OLLAMA_API_KEY=...
# or store it once in the macOS Keychain (the app looks up service "ferrite",
# account = the variable name; the command prompts for the value):
#   security add-generic-password -U -s ferrite -a OLLAMA_API_KEY -w
# Gemini fallback account:       FERRITE_GEMINI_API_KEY
# Twin encryption key account:   FERRITE_TWIN_KEY
